Improving Code Quality with SonarQube 💻
In any DevOps pipeline, maintaining clean, secure, and maintainable code is just as important as delivering fast. That's where SonarQube plays a crucial role.
🔍 Why SonarQube?
 SonarQube is an open-source platform that continuously inspects code for:
* Code smells
* Bugs
* Vulnerabilities
* Technical debt
* Code coverage (when integrated with test reports)

✅ Key Benefits I've seen in real projects:

- Early detection of issues before code hits production
- Seamless integration with Jenkins, GitHub Actions, and other CI/CD tools
- Supports multiple languages: Java, Python, JavaScript, and more
- Helps enforce coding standards across the team
- Improves collaboration between Devs, QA, and DevOps

🔧 My typical setup:

-->Code pushed to GitHub
-->Jenkins triggers a build
-->SonarQube scan runs as part of the pipeline
-->Results are visible in SonarQube dashboard
-->Build fails if quality gates are not met – helping us catch issues early!
